%% Dispose during an active gesture sequence
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber

  actor App as Application
  actor User as User pointer
  participant Surface as CanvasSurface
  participant Runtime as CanvasRuntime
  participant Tools as CanvasToolPort
  participant IE as InteractionEngine
  participant Preview as CanvasPreviewState
  participant Frame as FrameEngine
  participant Store as DocumentStoreKernel
  participant Spatial as SpatialKernel
  participant Projection as DocumentProjectionCache
  participant Resources as ResourceKernel
  participant Cache as ImageResolveCache
  participant Resolver as CanvasResourceResolver
  participant MoveResolver as CanvasMoveCommitResolver
  participant EK as EditKernel
  participant Actions as CanvasActionCommitted stream
  participant TextRequests as CanvasTextEditRequested stream
  participant Signals as Public signals

  Note over User,Preview: Initial condition: one active routed pointer owns a preview snapshot.
  Note over Store,Resources: Committed document, selection, spatial indexes, projection cache, and resource descriptors are current before dispose.

  App->>Runtime: dispose()

  alt runtime is already disposed
    Runtime-->>App: return without side effects
    Note over Runtime,Signals: Dispose is idempotent. No repaint, stream event, revision tick, resource invalidation, resolver call, or document read is produced.
  else first dispose call
    Runtime->>Runtime: enter disposing guard and reject reentrant mutation
    Runtime->>Tools: stop accepting new public pointer routing
    Tools->>IE: interrupt active pointer because runtime is disposing
    IE->>IE: classify active session as dispose cancellation
    Note over IE,MoveResolver: Move commit resolver is not called when dispose cancels a gesture.

    alt active preview is selected move
      IE->>Preview: clear selected move preview and active session
      IE->>Preview: bump overlayRevision for cleared active preview
      Preview->>Frame: request main-scene repaint cleanup
      Frame->>Store: capture committed frame facts and selection ids once
      Frame->>Preview: capture no selectedMoveDelta
      Frame->>Spatial: query viewport without preview-shifted selected supplement
      Spatial-->>Frame: ordinary candidate handles only
      Frame->>Signals: publish main repaint cleanup request
      Signals-->>Surface: repaint main scene without selected move preview
      Note over Preview,Frame: Selected move cleanup is main-scene cleanup, not overlay-only cleanup.
    else active preview is overlay-only
      IE->>Preview: clear overlay preview and active session
      IE->>Preview: bump overlayRevision for cleared active preview
      Preview->>Frame: request overlay repaint cleanup
      Frame->>Preview: capture no overlay preview primitive
      Frame->>Signals: publish overlay cleanup repaint request
      Signals-->>Surface: repaint overlay without preview
      Note over Preview,Frame: Marquee, pencil, marker, pending line, line preview, and eraser corridor cleanup target the overlay.
    end

    Runtime->>Resources: clear mandatory v1 runtime resource caches
    Resources->>Cache: drop resolved-image cache entries
    Note over Resources,Resolver: App-owned ui.Image instances and the app resolver are not disposed by the engine.

    Runtime->>Actions: close stream
    Runtime->>TextRequests: close stream
    Note over Runtime,Signals: No public listenable close is specified by v1. Dispose does not increment document revisions. overlayRevision advances only when dispose clears active preview.

    Runtime->>Runtime: transition to disposed
    Runtime-->>App: dispose complete

    Note over EK,Store: No terminal commit, no EditKernel commit, no DraftDocument, no TouchedSet, no CommitPlan, and no atomic install.
    Note over Store,Projection: No document revision, selection, spatial index, projection cache, or resource descriptor mutation occurs due solely to dispose.
    Note over Actions,Signals: No CanvasActionCommitted and no text edit request is emitted by dispose.
  end

  User->>Surface: later pointer move or terminal sample
  Surface->>Runtime: route public mutating operation
  Runtime-->>Surface: throw StateError("CanvasRuntime is disposed.")
  Note over Surface,IE: Later samples cannot revive the pointer session or commit a stale preview.

  App->>Runtime: readDocument()
  Runtime->>Store: read last committed immutable document
  Store-->>Runtime: last committed document
  Runtime-->>App: CanvasDocument

  App->>Runtime: later edit, command, selection, tool, camera, loadDocument, or resource mutation
  Runtime-->>App: throw StateError("CanvasRuntime is disposed.")
